pokeplatinum-saveptr.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies the patches in name order): no host pointer in a map object's
saved movement data. MapObject_Save copies each map object's two 16-byte movement-data buffers (unk_D8, unk_E8) into the
save as they are (MapObjectSave.unk_30, unk_40). Two movement types keep a pointer there:
 - UnkStruct_02069F48.unk_08, the MapObject a trainer follows (sub_02069DF4's type: the second trainer of a pair walks
   behind the first);
 - UnkStruct_0206A0BC.unk_04, the OverworldAnimManager of a hidden object's effect (sub_0206A104's types).
On the DS each is a 4-byte address; as a host pointer it is 8 bytes (UnkStruct_02069F48 grew from 12 to 16 bytes, still
inside the buffer) and the save held the host address: a Platinum save then differed by the build (the address of
libntr's s_HW_MAIN_MEM moves with the binary; clang 18 and clang 21 builds wrote different bytes at the same frame). Both
fields are now u32 DS-style addresses (port_plat.h PortPlat_DsAddr / PortPlat_HostAddr: the game's heaps lie in
s_HW_MAIN_MEM, an offset there is 0x02000000 + offset), so the structs have the DS's size and the save the same bytes on
every build. The game never reads the saved value back: each type's restore function clears it (sub_02069E50 sets
unk_01 = 0, so sub_02069F48 finds the partner again before unk_08 is read; sub_0206A168 sets unk_04 to NULL), so a save
written before this change (a host pointer in those 8 bytes) loads as before.

--- a/src/unk_02069BE0.c
+++ b/src/unk_02069BE0.c
@@ -36,5 +36,5 @@
     s16 unk_04;
     u16 unk_06;
-    MapObject *unk_08;
+    u32 unk_08; // the MapObject followed, as a DS address (PortPlat_DsAddr): saved with the map object (MapObjectSave.unk_30)
 } UnkStruct_02069F48;
 
@@ -44,5 +44,5 @@
     u8 unk_02;
     u8 unk_03;
-    OverworldAnimManager *unk_04;
+    u32 unk_04; // an OverworldAnimManager, as a DS address (PortPlat_DsAddr): saved with the map object
 } UnkStruct_0206A0BC;
 
@@ -370,10 +370,10 @@
     param1->unk_04 = MapObject_GetZ(param2);
     param1->unk_06 = 0xff;
-    param1->unk_08 = param2;
+    param1->unk_08 = PortPlat_DsAddr(param2);
 }
 
